From 035a21f5833966fc8093f314b9eee37de4debabf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(documents): redacted versions and discarded
 originals (PRV-016, ADR-0007)

- replace_with_redacted(): stores a worker-made redacted copy (JPEG/PNG, size limit) as the
  next version (queued -> normal malware scan via the outbox; usable evidence at once),
  makes it current and discards the original; audit document.version_redacted.
- discard_version(): the version stays as a row (quarantined, error aadhaar_redacted |
  aadhaar_unredactable; audit document.version_discarded) and its object is deleted after
  commit by the outbox task documents.discard_object (retries; refuses live versions and
  foreign keys) plus a daily sweep of the last 7 days.
- ObjectStore.discard(): tag sos-lifecycle=discarded, then delete, so the versioned bucket
  does not keep the bytes for the 90-day recovery window; lifecycle rule discarded-1d on the
  shared and dedicated files buckets expires tagged versions after one day.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
